From: MilkFlint4 <noreply@milkflint4.local>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: UL MU-MIMO / UL OFDMA module params

mt7996 already left cfg.mimo_ul_en and cfg.ofdma_ul_en clear (zeroed
TLV), so Flint 4 never enabled the scheduled-uplink path that stalls
AC_BE on MT7986. Expose muru_mimo_ul and muru_ofdma_ul (default off,
0644) so MilkFlint can opt in from userspace the same way mt7915 does
for UL OFDMA, without baking the flags on.

Signed-off-by: MilkFlint4 <noreply@milkflint4.local>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c	2026-11-21 19:42:14.968975896 +0000
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c	2026-11-21 23:41:57.710280993 +0000
@@ -108,6 +108,18 @@
 module_param(sr_scene_detect, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(sr_scene_detect, "Enable firmware scene detection algorithm");
 
+/* Off by default (same as the prior zeroed cfg flags). Opt in when several
+ * Wi-Fi 6/7 devices upload heavily at once; the firmware keeps the first
+ * station's setting per band until stations rejoin.
+ */
+static bool muru_mimo_ul;
+module_param(muru_mimo_ul, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(muru_mimo_ul, "Let the firmware schedule UL MU-MIMO for HE/EHT stations (default off; set before stations join)");
+
+static bool muru_ofdma_ul;
+module_param(muru_ofdma_ul, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(muru_ofdma_ul, "Let the firmware schedule UL OFDMA for HE/EHT stations (default off; set before stations join)");
+
 static u8
 mt7996_mcu_get_sta_nss(u16 mcs_map)
 {
@@ -1816,6 +1828,8 @@
 			       link_conf->vht_mu_beamformer ||
 			       link_conf->vht_mu_beamformee;
 	muru->cfg.ofdma_dl_en = true;
+	muru->cfg.mimo_ul_en = READ_ONCE(muru_mimo_ul);
+	muru->cfg.ofdma_ul_en = READ_ONCE(muru_ofdma_ul);
 
 	if (link_sta->vht_cap.vht_supported)
 		muru->mimo_dl.vht_mu_bfee =
